{"id":"bang-east-of-formosa-1944-09-20","title":"A convoy east of Formosa, 20–21 September 1944","short":"20–21 September 1944","eyebrow":"South of Honshu and east of Formosa · BANG's third war patrol","theater":"pacific","clock":"","window":{"from":"1944-09-20T04:00Z","to":"1944-09-20T20:00Z"},"gmt":true,"participants":[{"id":"bang","name":"BANG","side":"us","kind":"submarine","hull":"SS-385","co":"LCdr A. R. Gallaher","track":"ss-385-bang/3","sil":"balao","alias":"ss-385-bang","colour":1}],"places":[{"name":"Philippine Sea","lon":137.3,"lat":28.45},{"name":"Formosa","lon":121.6,"lat":24.4,"inset":[120.6,23.0]},{"name":"Yonaguni","lon":123.0,"lat":24.38,"small":true},{"name":"Iriomote","lon":123.82,"lat":24.2,"small":true},{"name":"Ishigaki","lon":124.17,"lat":24.3,"small":true},{"name":"Miyako","lon":125.3,"lat":24.6,"small":true},{"name":"Honshu","lon":138.3,"lat":35.6,"inset":[138.3,36.2]}],"sections":[{"heading":"","paras":[{"text":"BANG's last two attacks of her third patrol, on a convoy she found by its escorts' sound pinging, as typed on her attack sheets. No Japanese record of them has been found yet.","aside":false}]},{"heading":"Outcome","paras":[{"text":"No Japanese record found yet. BANG claimed an AO and an AK sunk and one damaged, as FRUPAC relayed it.","aside":false}]},{"heading":"The target","paras":[{"text":"BANG made contact by the escorts' JK sound pinging at 35,000 yards.","aside":false}]},{"heading":"Reading the map","paras":[{"text":"Positions are BANG's own dead reckoning and star sights; lines between them are straight, and where she went in between is not recorded. Open circles are ships she sighted, at the target's position. As the clock passes each firing time a red ring pulses at BANG's position; hover a diamond for the attack sheet.","aside":false}]},{"heading":"Clocks","paras":[{"text":"BANG kept zone K (−10) throughout. Japanese records use Tokyo time (I, −9).","aside":false}]},{"heading":"Records with no time","paras":[{"text":"Neither Japanese record for this patrol gives a time: combinedfleet.com's account of convoy No. 3905 and the 4th Surface Escort Division's daily summary for TAKA-909. Each is drawn at the time of the attack it matches, and marked so. FRUPAC's intercept has No. 3905's ships \"torp & sunk 1520/09\" (1520 I = 1620 K, between Attacks 1 and 2).","aside":false}]},{"heading":"What is missing","paras":[{"text":"No Japanese record has been found yet for Attacks 5 and 6 (20–21 September); the 4th Escort diary has no attack on those days. Where the Japanese record names only the ships that were hit, the rest of the convoy is described as BANG saw it.","aside":false}]},{"heading":"Sources","paras":[{"text":"BANG's third war patrol report, NARA microfilm M1752 (74802831). The 4th Surface Escort Division / Okinawa Base Force war diary, September 1944, via JACAR (C08030144100, National Institute for Defense Studies). Convoy No. 3905 from combinedfleet.com, a secondary source, flagged where used. Coastline: Natural Earth.","aside":false}]}],"cites":{},"box":[122.6,24.817,124.317,25.65],"tracks":{"bang":[{"who":"bang","utc":"1944-09-19T20:51Z","lat":24.0,"lon":122.0,"kind":"bt","ref":"BT","on_track":true,"local":"1944-09-19 2051 Z","raw":"24-00N 122-00E","note":"","fix":"","assumed":false,"cite":{"ref":"rg367-74802831/p28","href":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0073.jpg","label":"p. 28","source_title":"nara-catalog"}},{"who":"bang","utc":"1944-09-20T14:15Z","lat":25.35,"lon":123.9667,"kind":"attack","ref":"Attack 5","on_track":true,"local":"1944-09-21 0015 K","raw":"25-21N 123-58E","note":"Torpedo attack No. 5","fix":"","assumed":false,"cite":{"ref":"rg367-74802831/p21","href":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0066.jpg","label":"p. 21","source_title":"nara-catalog"}},{"who":"bang","utc":"1944-09-20T14:17Z","l